description: Hindsight ambient memory vs Obsidian durable documents — boundaries
alwaysApply: true
---

Treat Hindsight and Obsidian as complementary, not duplicates.

If Hindsight is missing, install the **official** Cursor plugin (`pip install hindsight-cursor` && `hindsight-cursor init`) — do not hand-roll or vendor a fork. See [Hindsight Cursor docs](https://hindsight.vectorize.io/sdks/integrations/cursor).

## Hindsight (automatic ambient memory)

Stores short durable facts across sessions via official hooks + MCP:

- Decisions and rationale
- Working preferences
- Project context
- Important discoveries
- Topic relationships
- Corrections / superseded assumptions

Hooks (no manual commands needed):

- `sessionStart` → auto-recall into context
- `stop` / `sessionEnd` → auto-retain

MCP tools (`recall`, `retain`, `reflect`) are for mid-session use when switching topics or researching something new — call them when relevant, not on every trivial turn.

Config: `~/.hindsight/cursor.json`. Local daemon: `http://127.0.0.1:9077`, bank `cursor`.

## Obsidian wiki (durable documents)

Owns long-form, citable knowledge under `obsidian/{{PROJECT}}/`:

- Research, playbooks, meeting notes, reference material
- Follow `AGENTS.md` for ingest/query/lint

## Boundaries

- Do NOT copy full Obsidian pages into Hindsight.
- Do NOT rewrite the vault from Hindsight memories.
- Prefer filing detailed research into the wiki; let Hindsight keep the working residue (preferences, decisions, open threads).
- When topic-switching or starting deep research: use Hindsight `recall` for prior decisions/preferences, then read `wiki/index.md` / search the vault for documents.
